WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Could oral antibiotics replace six weeks of intravenous therapy for bone and joint infection?

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
OVIVA randomized 1054 adults at 26 U.K. sites.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Definite treatment failure at 1 year: 13.2% with oral therapy.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Risk difference minus 1.4 percentage points, 90% CI -4.9 to 2.2, inside the 7.5-point noninferiority margin.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Catheter complications: 1.0% with oral versus 9.4% with intravenous.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Median hospital stay: 11 days oral versus 14 days intravenous.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Oral therapy was noninferior. N Engl J Med, 2019. Scroll for the full breakdown.
